A guard clause never behaves as the programmer expects. Which line is the bug?
void check(int flag) {
    if (flag = 0)
        reset();
    return;
}

This C program must read an integer into x and print it. Which line prevents that?
int main(void) {
    int x;
    scanf("%d", x);
    printf("%d\n", x);
    return 0;
}

Array a has exactly n elements, indexed 0 through n-1. The loop below is meant to sum them all. Which line reads outside the array?
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++)
    sum += a[i];
printf("%d", sum);

A program copies user input into an 8-byte buffer, buf. Which line lets very long input write past the end of the array?
char buf[8];
scanf("%s", buf);
puts(buf);
return 0;

This function is supposed to print a running total, but it prints an unpredictable number. Which line is the bug?
int total;
printf("%d\n", total);
return 0;
}
